    "narrative": "For LawDog, **Daulton Varsho** (61.26) stands out as our premier start today. Despite the potential #8 spot in the lineup, his favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Seth Lugo and high base projection override the order penalty. While **Yainer Diaz** (58.67) and **Kyle Karros** (57.59) remain strong plays, **Varsho** offers the best path to offensive production given the matchup context. **Karros** is particularly interesting; despite hitting against a solid arm in Michael King, his favorable park factors and the +10% boost from the opposing pitcher's profile make him a core contributor to our daily floor. We are keeping a close watch on **Yainer Diaz**, **Bryce Harper**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Braden Montgomery**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Justin Crawford**, as all are currently pending official lineup confirmation; any shifts in their batting order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their final efficiency scores.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision was omitting **Zack Gelof** (38.33). He finished just shy of our 40.0 \"marginal\" threshold, largely due to a difficult matchup against Rasmussen (3.30 xERA) and negative park factors that dragged his base projection down. While **Gelof** has the pedigree, the optimizer correctly prioritized the higher-upside profiles of **Alex Freeland** and **Jonathan Aranda**, who benefit from superior platoon configurations today. We are also monitoring **Justin Crawford** closely; while his 47.86 score earns him a start, he is dangerously close to the bottom of our playable tier. With **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Tyler Freeman** unavailable due to off-days or minor league assignments, our depth is thin, placing the burden of scoring on **Bryce Harper** and **Jonathan Aranda** to provide the necessary power and contact to keep us competitive in the 5x5 race.",
